aybook is meant for a role.\n\nNow, I\'ll draft each task step by step, ensuring the correct module names and parameters. I\'ll make sure the YAML is valid, using proper indentation and line breaks. Also, I\'ll check that each task is included conditionally where necessary, like the optional tasks.\n\nFinally, I\'ll compile all these tasks into a single YAML playbook, starting with \'---\' and ensuring it\'s valid for an Ansible Role.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: check if all variables have been set correctly\n  ansible.builtin.assert:\n    that: var1 is defined and var2 is defined\n    fail_on_any: yes\n  vars:\n    var1: "{{ var1 | default(\'not_set\') }}"\n    var2: "{{ var2 | default(\'not_set\') }}"\n\n- name: wait for host (when configured)\n  ansible.builtin.metadata:\n    wait_for: true\n  when: bootstrap_wait_for_host\n\n- name: prepare system\n  ansible.builtin.ansible:\n    module_name: setup\n    gather_facts: yes\n  register: setup_result\n  ignore_errors: yes\n  changed_when: false\n\n- name: include tasks to gather bootstrap facts (raw)\n  ansible.builtin.include_tasks:\n    file: tasks/bootstrap_facts_raw.yml\n\n- name: install bootstrap packages (raw)\n  ansible.builtin.raw:\n    cmd: "{{ bootstrap_install.raw | default(\'echo no packages to install\') }}"\n  when: ansible_os_family == "RedHat" or ansible_os_family == "Debian"\n\n- name: ensure system is prepared by issuing ansible modules\n  ansible.builtin.ansible:\n    module_name: package\n    args: "{{ packages_to_install | default([]) | json_query(\'[]\') | join(\' \') }}"\n  when: ansible_os_family == "RedHat" or ansible_os_family == "Debian"\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-02T08:08:39.104934495Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 13596128805, 'load_duration': 98518165, 'prompt_eval_count': 492, 'prompt_eval_duration': 110177531, 'eval_count': 835, 'eval_duration': 13385962056, 'model_name': 'deepseek