sk includes updating packages and installing yum-utils if needed. Using the yum module, I'll ensure yum is updated and that yum-utils is installed. Then, notify reboot.\n\nFinally, Task 7 uses zypper for updates. The task is straightforward, so I'll use the zypper module to update and notify reboot.\n\nI need to ensure all tasks are ordered correctly as per the given sequence. Each task should have the correct module and parameters. Also, the notify parameter points to a reboot handler, which I assume is defined elsewhere in the role.\n\nI'll structure each task with a name, action, and any necessary parameters. Each task will be a YAML block under the tasks key. I'll make sure there's a line break after each task for proper YAML formatting.\n\nI should also check for any potential issues, like ensuring that the files exist where they're being imported or used. For example, assert.yml should be present in files/. But that's beyond the scope of the playbook itself.\n\nPutting it all together, I'll start with '---' followed by the tasks in order, each with their respective modules and parameters, and the necessary notifications.\n</think>\n\n```\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  import_tasks:\n    file: files/assert.yml\n    remote_host: localhost\n\n- name: Configure apk\n  become: yes\n  become_user: root\n  apt:\n    name: apk\n    state: present\n  shell: apk update && apk upgrade\n  notify: reboot\n\n- name: Configure apt\n  become: yes\n  become_user: root\n  apt:\n    name: apt\n    state: present\n  apt:\n    action: upgrade\n    state: upgrade\n  shell: apt autoremove --unused\n  notify: reboot\n\n- name: Update all software (dnf)\n  become: yes\n  become_user: root\n  dnf:\n    name: '*'\n    state: present\n    exclude: kernel*\n  notify: reboot\n\n- name: Update all software (pacman)\n  become: yes\n  become_user: root\n  pacman:\n    name: '*'\n    state: present\n  notify: reboot\n\n- name: Configure yum\n  become: yes\n  become_user: root\n  yum:\n    