ord_validity.stat\' is a dictionary, and comparing it to a string \'365\' is incorrect. But the error is about truthy values, so perhaps the comparison is causing a type error, but the yamllint error is about the \'when\' clause expecting a boolean.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the \'when\' clause is using an expression that returns a non-boolean. So, we need to ensure that the expression evaluates to a boolean.\n\nWait, \'user.password_validity_days is defined\' is a boolean, and \'password_validity.stat | default(\'\')\' is a string, but comparing it to \'365\' might not be the right approach. Maybe the \'stat\' module returns a dictionary, and we need to check a specific field, like \'password_validity_days\'.\n\nWait, in the \'stat\' module, when you run \'ansible.builtin.stat\' with a path, it returns information about the file. But in Task 8, it\'s used to get the home directory, so \'stat\' is used on a user\'s home. Then, in Task 14, it\'s trying to check the password validity days, which is in \'/etc/shadow\', but the \'stat\' module on a user\'s home directory doesn\'t give that info. So, Task 14 is incorrect because it\'s using \'password_validity.stat\', which is from the home directory\'s stat, not the password info.\n\nWait, that\'s a functional issue, but the yamllint error is about truthy values. So, perhaps the \'when\' clause is using an incorrect expression.\n\nIn any case, the \'when\' clause in Task 14 is using \'password_validity.stat | default(\'\') != \'365\'\' which is comparing a string (from default) to \'365\', but the \'stat\' result is a dictionary, so this comparison is invalid. So, the \'when\' clause is incorrect, leading to a truthy value error.\n\nSo, to fix this, perhaps Task 14 should use a different approach, maybe using the \'user_stat\' module or another way to get the password validity days.\n\nBut since the user\'s instruction is to only fix the yamllint errors and not change functionality, I need to adjust the \'when\' clause to use a boolean expression.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the \'when\' clause should be using \'user.password_validity_days is defined\' and \'password_validity.stat\' is truthy.\n\nBut this is getting complicated. Maybe the best approach is to ensure that all \'when\' conditions are using boolean expressions.\n\nSo, in summary, the main issues are:\n\n1. In Task 12, the \'when\' clause uses \'user.copy_private_key | default(\'no\')\', which is a string, leading to a truthy value error. We should change it to \'user.copy_private_key | bool\' or \'user.copy_private_key is defined\'.\n\n2. In Task 14, the \'when\' clause is using an incorrect comparison, leading to a truthy value error. We should adjust the expression to properly check the password validity days.\n\n3. The line length in Task 14 is too long, exceeding 80 characters.\n\nSo, to fix these:\n\n- For Task 12: Change \'when: user.copy_private_key | default(\'no\')\' to \'when: user.copy_private_key | bool\'.\n\n- For Task 14: Simplify the \'when\' clause to check if \'user.password_validity_days\' is defined and the current validity is not 365. Also, break the line to adhere to the 80 character limit.\n\nAdditionally, I\'ll check other \'when\' clauses to ensure they\'re using boolean expressions.\n\nNow, I\'ll rewrite the playbook with these fixes.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Create local ssh_key_directory for {{ user.name }}\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: "{{ ansible_env.HOME }}/.ssh"\n    state: directory\n    mode: 0750\n  when: user.manage_ssh_key\n  run_once: true\n\n- name: Manage user {{ user.name }}\n  ansible.builtin.user:\n    name: "{{ user.name }}"\n    state: "{{ user.state | default(\'present\') }}"\n    password: "{{ user.password | default(\'\') | password_hash(\'sha512\') }}"\n    sudoable: "{{ user.sudoable | default(\'yes\') }}"\n    shell: "{{ user.shell | default(\'/bin/bash\') }}"\n    comment: "{{ user.comment | default(\'\') }}"\n    system_user: "{{ user.system_user | default(\'no\') }}"\n    groups: "{{ user.groups | default(\'\') }}"\n\n- name: Set sudo options for {{ user.name }}\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: "/etc/sudoers.d/{{ user.name }}"\n    state: present\n    content: "{{ user.sudo_options | default(\'\') }}"\n    mode: 0640\n  when: user.sudo_options is defined\n  register: sudoers_file\n\n- name: Remove sudo options for {{ user.name }}\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: "/etc/sudoers.d/{{ user.name }}"\n    state: absent\n  when: not user.sudo_options\n\n- name: Generate private ssh key for {{ user.name }}\n  ansible.builtin.ssh_keygen:\n    generate_private_key: yes\n    key_name: "{{ user.name }}_ssh"\n    private_key_file: "~/.ssh/{{ user.name }}_ssh"\n    public_key_file: "~/.ssh/{{ user.name }}_ssh.pub"\n    key_type: rsa\n    size: 2048\n  when: user.manage_ssh_key\n  run_once: true\n\n- name: Generate public ssh key for {{ user.name }}\n  ansible.builtin.ssh_keygen:\n    generate_public_key: yes\n    key_name: "{{ user.name }}_ssh"\n    public_key_file: "~/.ssh/{{ user.name }}_ssh.pub"\n  when: user.manage_ssh_key\n  run_once: true\n\n- name: Convert ssh key to ppk for {{ user.name }}\n  ansible.builtin.ssh_keygen:\n    convert_to_ssh_dot_com: yes\n    key_name: "{{ user.name }}_ssh"\n    ppk_file: "~/.ssh/{{ user.name }}_ssh.ppk"\n  when: user.manage_ssh_key\n  run_once: true\n\n- name: Get or set the home directory for {{ user.name }}\n  ansible.builtin.stat:\n    path: "{{ user.name }}"\n  register: user_home\n  run_once: true\n\n- name: Create .ssh directory for {{ user.name }}\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: "{{ ansible_env.HOME }}/.ssh"\n    state: directory\n    mode: 0750\n  when: user.manage_ssh_key or user.private_keys | default([]) | length > 0\n\n- name: Deploy authorized keys for {{ user.name }}\n  ansible.builtin.authorized_key:\n    user: "{{ user.name }}"\n    state: present\n    key: "{{ key }}"\n    path: "~/.ssh/authorized_keys"\n    manage_dir: yes\n    mode: 0600\n  loop: "{{ user.authorized_keys | default([]) }}"\n\n- name: Remove unauthorized keys for {{ user.name }}\n  ansible.builtin.authorized_key:\n    user: "{{ user.name }}"\n    state: absent\n    key: "{{ key }}"\n    path: "~/.ssh/authorized_keys"\n  loop: "{{ user.unauthorized_keys | default([]) }}"\n\n- name: Copy generated private ssh key for {{ user.name }}\n  ansible.builtin.copy:\n    content: "{{ lookup(\'file\', \'~/.ssh/{{ user.name }}_ssh\') }}"\n    dest: "{{ ansible_env.HOME }}/.ssh/"\n    mode: 0600\n    remote_src: yes\n  when: user.copy_private_key | bool\n\n- name: Place private key file for {{ user.name }}\n  ansible.builtin.copy:\n    content: "{{ lookup(\'file\', \'~/.ssh/{{ user.name }}_ssh\') }}"\n    dest: "{{ ansible_env.HOME }}/.ssh/"\n    mode: 0600\n    remote_src: yes\n  when: user.private_keys | default([]) | length > 0\n\n- name: Check users password valid time for {{ user.name }}\n  ansible.builtin.stat:\n    path: "/etc/shadow"\n    name: "{{ user.name }}"\n  register: password_validity\n  run_once: true\n\n- name: Set users password valid time for {{ user.name }}\n  ansible.builtin.user:\n    name: "{{ user.name }}"\n    password_validity_days: "{{ user.password_validity_days | default(\'365\') }}"\n  when: user.password_validity_days is defined and (password_validity.stat | default({}) | dictget(\'pw_validity_days\') != 365)\n\n- name: Create .ssh directory for {{ user.name }}\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: "{{ ansible_env.HOME }}/.ssh"\n    state: directory\n    mode: 0750\n  when: user.manage_ssh_key or user.private_keys | default([]) | length > 0\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-02T09:25:08.383272538Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 93646109080, 'load_duration': 106444706, 'prompt_eval_count': 2243, 'prompt_eval_duration': 855184959, 'eval_count': 3968, 'eval_duration': 92683732257, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--90bde99a-ceca-4130-87a1-0e64d464a