content='<think>\nOkay, I need to create an Ansible Playbook based on the given tasks. The user has specified 13 tasks, each with specific descriptions and requirements. Let me go through each task one by one to ensure I understand what\'s needed.\n\nFirst, the playbook must start with \'---\' on the very first line, so I\'ll make sure to include that. It should be a valid YAML file, conforming to yamllint and ansible-lint standards. Also, it\'s meant to be part of an Ansible Role under the tasks directory, so I don\'t need playbook-level headers like hosts or vars.\n\nTask 1: Import assert.yml. This should be a block with import_tasks, only run once on localhost. So I\'ll set the localhost host and use import_tasks.\n\nTask 2: Install apache httpd using httpd_packages. I\'ll use apt or yum depending on the OS, but since it\'s a variable, I\'ll use the package module with name: httpd_packages.\n\nTask 3: Configure SELinux. I\'ll use the setsebool module, checking if SELinux is enabled. The boolean values come from variables, so I\'ll set them conditionally.\n\nTask 4: Configure httpd with a template. I\'ll use template module, specifying src and dest, and notify the handler for restart.\n\nTask 5: Activate httpd modules on Debian. I\'ll use command a2enmod for each module, then notify the handler.\n\nTask 6: Import ssl.yml if HTTPS is enabled. I\'ll use import_tasks with conditionals.\n\nTask 7: Import locations.yml if there are locations. Again, conditional import.\n\nTask 8: Import vhosts.yml if virtual hosts are defined.\n\nTask 9: Configure ports on Debian or Suse. Use template and notify handler if OS is correct.\n\nTask 10: Import directories.yml if directories are defined.\n\nTask 11: Flush handlers to execute them after all tasks.\n\nTask 12: Remove default index.html if variable is true.\n\nTask 13: Start and enable httpd service using the variable.\n\nI need to structure each task correctly, using the right modules and variables. Also, ensure that all tasks are in the correct order and that conditionals are applied where necessary. I should avoid adding any extra tasks or modifying the order. The playbook should only contain the tasks as described, without any comments or explanations, just valid YAML.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  block:\n    - import_tasks: assert.yml\n  hosts: localhost\n  run_once: true\n\n- name: Install apache httpd\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ httpd_packages }}"\n    state: present\n  yum:\n    name: "{{ httpd_packages }}"\n    state: present\n  become: yes\n\n- name: Configure selinux\n  setsebool:\n    name: "{{ item }}"\n    value: "{{ item_value }}"\n  loop: "{{ httpd_selinuxBOOLENS | default([]) }}"\n\n- name: Configure httpd\n  template:\n    src: "{{ httpd_template_src }}"\n    dest: "{{ httpd_template_dest }}"\n  notify: httpd_test_and_restart\n\n- name: Activate httpd module | Debian\n  command: a2enmod "{{ item }}"\n  loop: "{{ httpd_enable_modules | default([]) }}"\n  notify: httpd_test_and_restart\n\n- name: Import ssl.yml\n  import_tasks: ssl.yml\n  when: https_ssl_enabled | default(false)\n\n- name: Import locations.yml\n  import_tasks: locations.yml\n  when: locations_defined | default(false)\n\n- name: Import vhosts.yml\n  import_tasks: vhosts.yml\n  when: vhosts_defined | default(false)\n\n- name: Configure ports\n  template:\n    src: "{{ httpd_ports_src }}"\n    dest: "{{ httpd_ports_dest }}"\n  notify: httpd_test_and_restart\n  when: ansible_distribution in [\'debian\', \'suse\']\n\n- name: Import directories.yml\n  import_tasks: directories.yml\n  when: directories_defined | default(false)\n\n- name: Flush handlers\n  meta: flush_handlers\n\n- name: Removing default html\n  file:\n    path: "{{ httpd_default_html_path }}"\n    state: absent\n  when: httpd_remove_example | default(false)\n\n- name: Start and enable httpd\n  service:\n    name: "{{ httpd_service }}"\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n  become: yes\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-02T09:37:17.898207003Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 19913829473, 'load_duration': 99268870, 'prompt_eval_count': 653, 'prompt_eval_duration': 402875137, 'eval_count': 931, 'eval_duration': 19410529971, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--e0a178db-01fa-4be6-ab81-c48a10bcf4ce-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 653, 'output_tokens': 931, 'total_tokens': 1584}
