content='<think>\nAlright, I need to generate an Ansible Playbook based on the user\'s instructions. Let me go through each step carefully.\n\nFirst, the user specified that the playbook must start with \'---\' on the very first line. I\'ll make sure to include that without any additional text or formatting.\n\nNext, the playbook needs to be a valid YAML file that adheres to yamllint and ansible-lint standards. I\'ll structure each task correctly, ensuring proper indentation and syntax.\n\nThe playbook should be structured for an Ansible Role, meaning it should be placed in the tasks/ directory, likely as tasks/main.yml. So, I\'ll organize the tasks in the correct order without any playbook-level headers like hosts: or vars:.\n\nThere are five tasks to include, each with specific requirements:\n\n1. **Task 1**: Check if certificates exist using the `java_cert` module with the `certificate` parameter set to the `java_certs` variable.\n\n2. **Task 2**: Fail if any certificate is missing. I\'ll use the `fail` module with `msg` indicating the missing certificates.\n\n3. **Task 3**: Set `java_keystore_dir` based on `java_keystore_dir_old` if `java_open_jdk_version_major` is less than 11. This uses `set_fact` with a conditional `when`.\n\n4. **Task 4**: Set `java_keystore_dir` using `java_keystore_dir_new` if the version is 11 or higher. Again, using `set_fact` with a condition.\n\n5. **Task 5**: Import SSL certificates into the Java keystore using the `java_cert` module with `action` set to \'import\'.\n\nI need to ensure each task is in the correct order and uses the exact module calls and parameters specified. I\'ll avoid adding any extra tasks or modifying the existing ones.\n\nFinally, I\'ll structure the YAML without any comments or explanations, just the tasks as specified. Each task will have the correct YAML syntax, with proper indentation and line breaks.\n\nLet me piece it all together step by step, making sure each part aligns with the user\'s instructions and maintains the validity of the playbook within an Ansible Role.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Check if certificates exist\n  java_cert:\n    certificate: "{{ item }}"\n    state: present\n    validate_certs: no\n  loop: "{{ java_certs }}"\n  register: cert_status\n\n- name: Fail if some certificate doesn\'t exist\n  fail:\n    msg: "Certificate(s) not found: {{ missing_certs | join(\', \') }}"\n  when: cert_status.results | selectattr(\'failed\') | list | count > 0\n\n- name: Setting keystore variables in java < 11\n  set_fact:\n    java_keystore_dir: "{{ java_keystore_dir_old }}"\n  when: java_open_jdk_version_major < 11\n\n- name: Setting keystore variables in java >= 11\n  set_fact:\n    java_keystore_dir: "{{ java_keystore_dir_new }}"\n  when: java_open_jdk_version_major >= 11\n\n- name: Import SSL certificates\n  java_cert:\n    certificate: "{{ item.cert }}"\n    alias: "{{ item.alias | default(\'default\') }}"\n    keystore_path: "{{ java_open_jdk_home }}/{{ java_keystore_dir }}/cacerts"\n    action: import\n    state: present\n    validate_certs: no\n  loop: "{{ java_certs }}"\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-02T09:50:43.162288542Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 16728361726, 'load_duration': 93789088, 'prompt_eval_count': 499, 'prompt_eval_duration': 129707074, 'eval_count': 727, 'eval_duration': 16503576654, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--1619de59-f9a4-412d-9951-40dddb177487-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 499, 'output_tokens': 727, 'total_tokens': 1226}
