n Ansible, \'when\' can be a single condition or a list. So I\'ll keep it as is.\n\nAnother approach is to check the YAML structure. The playbook starts with \'---\' and each task is a list item. The \'when\' is correctly under each task.\n\nAfter reviewing, the main issues are:\n\n1. The \'when\' conditions are causing truthy errors because the linter expects boolean values, but they\'re correctly written as conditions.\n\n2. There\'s an extra blank line at the end causing the empty-lines error.\n\nTo fix the blank line, I\'ll remove any trailing newlines after the last task.\n\nFor the \'when\' conditions, perhaps the linter is being too strict, but to adhere to the linter, I\'ll ensure the \'when\' is correctly formatted. Maybe the issue is that the \'when\' is not a boolean but a condition. So, I\'ll leave it as is since it\'s correct in Ansible.\n\nSo, the corrected playbook will have the same tasks but with proper YAML formatting, removing the extra blank line and ensuring all tasks are correctly indented.\n\nI\'ll go through each task and adjust the YAML accordingly.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Create the RKE2 config directory\n  file:\n    path: /etc/rke2\n    state: directory\n\n- name: Set server taints\n  kubernetes_node_taints:\n    taints: "{{ rke2_node_taints | default([]) | list }}"\n  when: rke2_type == \'server\'\n\n- name: Set agent taints\n  kubernetes_node_taints:\n    taints: "{{ rke2_node_taints | default([]) | list }}"\n  when: rke2_type == \'agent\'\n\n- name: Copy RKE2 config file\n  copy:\n    src: /path/to/rke2.yaml\n    dest: /etc/rke2/rke2.yaml\n    remote_src: no\n  notify: rke2_config_changed\n\n- name: Copy kubelet config file\n  copy:\n    src: /path/to/kubelet.yaml\n    dest: /etc/rke2/kubelet.yaml\n    remote_src: no\n    condition: rke2_kubelet is not empty\n  notify: kubelet_config_changed\n\n- name: Copy Containerd Registry Configuration file\n  copy:\n    src: /path/to/containerd-registry.yaml\n    dest: /etc/rke2/containerd-registry.yaml\n    remote_src: no\n    condition: rke2_containerd is not empty\n  notify: containerd_config_changed\n\n- name: Start RKE2 service\n  service:\n    name: rke2\n    state: started\n    enabled: true\n  become: true\n  become_user: root\n\n- name: Mask other RKE2 services\n  service:\n    name: "{{ item }}"\n    state: stopped\n    enabled: false\n  with_items: "{{ rke2_other_services | default([]) | list }}"\n  when: rke2_type in [\'server\', \'agent\']\n\n- name: Wait for remaining nodes to be ready - no CNI\n  pause:\n    state: waiting\n    seconds: 60\n    until: "{{ node_ready_without_cni | default(0) | int }}"\n    retries: 3\n\n- name: Wait for remaining nodes to be ready - with CNI\n  pause:\n    state: waiting\n    seconds: 60\n    until: "{{ node_ready_with_cni | default(0) | int }}"\n    retries: 3\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-02T10:27:57.351270655Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 25273745113, 'load_duration': 94197566, 'prompt_eval_count': 1205, 'prompt_eval_duration': 502425039, 'eval_count': 1684, 'eval_duration': 24675577753, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--4271644c-b26a-480b-86fe-f50d94888216-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1205, 'output_tokens': 1684, 'total_tokens': 2889}
