st two tasks use the pause module to wait for nodes to be ready. They have until and retries parameters set correctly. No issues here.\n\nAfter reviewing all tasks, I\'ll ensure that the YAML syntax is correct. This includes proper indentation, correct use of colons, and no trailing spaces. The playbook should now be valid according to yamllint and ansible-lint.\n\nFinally, I\'ll present the corrected YAML playbook, ensuring that only the necessary changes are made to fix the linting errors without altering the intended functionality of the tasks.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Create the RKE2 config directory\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: /etc/rke2\n    state: directory\n    mode: 755\n\n- name: Set server taints\n  kubernetes_node_taints:\n    taints: "{{ rke2_node_taints | default([]) | list }}"\n  when: rke2_type == \'server\'\n\n- name: Set agent taints\n  kubernetes_node_taints:\n    taints: "{{ rke2_node_taints | default([]) | list }}"\n  when: rke2_type == \'agent\'\n\n- name: Copy RKE2 config file\n  ansible.builtin.copy:\n    src: /path/to/rke2.yaml\n    dest: /etc/rke2/rke2.yaml\n    remote_src: false\n    mode: 755\n  notify: rke2_config_changed\n\n- name: Copy kubelet config file\n  ansible.builtin.copy:\n    src: /path/to/kubelet.yaml\n    dest: /etc/rke2/kubelet.yaml\n    remote_src: false\n    condition: rke2_kubelet | bool\n    mode: 755\n  notify: kubelet_config_changed\n\n- name: Copy Containerd Registry Configuration file\n  ansible.builtin.copy:\n    src: /path/to/containerd-registry.yaml\n    dest: /etc/rke2/containerd-registry.yaml\n    remote_src: false\n    condition: rke2_containerd | bool\n    mode: 755\n  notify: containerd_config_changed\n\n- name: Start RKE2 service\n  ansible.builtin.service:\n    name: rke2\n    state: started\n    enabled: true\n    mode: 755\n\n- name: Mask other RKE2 services\n  ansible.builtin.service:\n    name: "{{ item }}"\n    state: stopped\n    enabled: false\n    with_items: "{{ rke2_other_services | default([]) | list }}"\n    when: rke2_type in [\'server\', \'agent\']\n\n- name: Wait for remaining nodes to be ready - no CNI\n  ansible.builtin.pause:\n    state: waiting\n    seconds: 60\n    until: "{{ node_ready_without_cni | default(0) | int }}"\n    retries: 3\n\n- name: Wait for remaining nodes to be ready - with CNI\n  ansible.builtin.pause:\n    state: waiting\n    seconds: 60\n    until: "{{ node_ready_with_cni | default(0) | int }}"\n    retries: 3\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-02T10:30:26.214478479Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 23306015629, 'load_duration': 100385140, 'prompt_eval_count': 1190, 'prompt_eval_duration': 650696987, 'eval_count': 1099, 'eval_duration': 22554018637, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--a3cf6ac2-8727-4aa7-8a4c-d46483aa7f17-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1190, 'output_tokens': 1099, 'total_tokens': 2289}
