able names and conditions are correct. Also, verify that the shell command is correctly capturing the output and that the debug task is correctly referencing it.\n\nFinally, I\'ll make sure the entire structure is valid according to yamllint and ansible-lint standards, as per the instructions. This should result in a correct and functional Ansible Playbook.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Ensure the summary block runs only on the first RKE2 server\n  shell: echo "Running summary block on first RKE2 server"\n  when: ansible_hostname == groups.rke2_servers[0]\n\n- name: Prepare summary of Kubernetes nodes\n  shell: kubectl get nodes -owide --kubeconfig /etc/rANCHER/kubeconfig\n  register: nodes_summary\n\n- name: Display the stdout_lines of the nodes summary\n  debug:\n    msg: "{{ ansible_host }} - Node summary: {{ nodes_summary.stdout_lines }}"\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-02T10:42:24.498798987Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 13731877112, 'load_duration': 101644657, 'prompt_eval_count': 355, 'prompt_eval_duration': 104887757, 'eval_count': 632, 'eval_duration': 13524219159, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--f99ae46e-9399-4acc-9b7f-9abee983e73a-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 355, 'output_tokens': 632, 'total_tokens': 987}
