it_for_pods) are correct and if the parameters match the requirements. For example, the service module\'s name parameter should be set to the variable rke2_service_name, and the wait parameter should be set to yes for the check mode.\n\nFinally, I\'ll structure the playbook starting with \'---\' followed by the tasks in the specified order. Each task should be a YAML block with the correct module, parameters, and any other necessary settings like delegate_to or state.\n\nI think I\'ve covered all the requirements. Now, I\'ll format the playbook accordingly, ensuring it\'s valid and meets all the user\'s instructions.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Restart RKE2 service on {{ rke2_node_name }}\n  ansible.builtin.service:\n    name: "{{ rke2_service_name }}"\n    state: restarted\n  delegate_to: "{{ rke2_node_name }}"\n\n- name: Wait for all nodes to be ready again\n  kubernetes.core.wait_for_nodes:\n    state: present\n    wait: yes\n    timeout: 100\n    interval: 15\n  delegate_to: "{{ active_server | default(first_server_in_group)}}"\n\n- name: Wait for all pods to be ready again\n  kubernetes.core.wait_for_pods:\n    state: present\n    wait: yes\n    timeout: 100\n    interval: 15\n  delegate_to: "{{ active_server | default(first_server_in_group)}}"\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-02T10:53:20.609944342Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 14651912096, 'load_duration': 78322353, 'prompt_eval_count': 502, 'prompt_eval_duration': 148623761, 'eval_count': 741, 'eval_duration': 14423039780, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--312c661a-13c2-4d0a-a144-536ad6b99c07-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 502, 'output_tokens': 741, 'total_tokens': 1243}
