er indentation and no extra comments or explanations beyond what\'s necessary.\n\nFinally, I\'ll review the playbook to ensure it starts with \'---\', follows YAML and Ansible standards, and accurately reflects each task\'s requirements without any deviations.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: enable_backports\n  apt_repository:\n    repo: "deb http://deb.debian.org/debian-backports/ {{ ansible_distribution_release }}-backports main"\n    state: present\n    filename: "backports-{{ ansible_distribution_release }}"\n    update_cache: yes\n\n- name: set_default_release\n  set_fact:\n    ansible_default_release: "{{ ansible_distribution_release }}-backports"\n  when: ansible_distribution_version < "9"\n\n- name: install_ansible\n  apt:\n    name: ansible\n    state: "{{ ansible_package_state }}"\n    default_release: "{{ ansible_default_release }}"\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-02T11:08:42.809474892Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 9466742489, 'load_duration': 80033677, 'prompt_eval_count': 401, 'prompt_eval_duration': 96386870, 'eval_count': 596, 'eval_duration': 9289423424, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--83d0117c-65b0-485a-bba3-aa4fca941898-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 401, 'output_tokens': 596, 'total_tokens': 997}
