 need to make sure each task is correctly ordered and uses the right modules. Also, variables like rsyslog_features and rsyslog_additional_configs should be properly referenced. I\'ll structure each task with the correct YAML syntax, using become where necessary, and ensure the playbook starts with ---.\n\nI think that\'s all. Now, I\'ll put it all together in the YAML format as specified.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  shell: ansible-playbook assert.yml\n\n- name: Uninstall conflicting systemd-logger\n  apt:\n    name: systemd-logger\n    state: absent\n\n- name: Install rsyslog\n  apt:\n    name: rsyslog\n    state: present\n    become: yes\n\n- name: Install additional rsyslog packages\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ item }}"\n    state: present\n    become: yes\n  with_items: "{{ rsyslog_features }}"\n\n- name: Configuring default rsyslog\n  template:\n    src: default_config.j2\n    dest: /etc/rsyslog.conf\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 755\n  when: rsyslog_deploy_default_config is true\n\n- name: Make configuration directory\n  file:\n    path: /etc/rsyslog.d/\n    state: directory\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 755\n\n- name: Configuring rsyslog forward rule\n  template:\n    src: forward_rule.j2\n    dest: /etc/rsyslog.d/50-forward.conf\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 755\n  when: rsyslog_deploy_default_config is false\n\n- name: Configuring additional config files\n  copy:\n    src: "{{ item.src }}"\n    dest: /etc/rsyslog.d/{{ item.dest }}\n    owner: "{{ item.owner }}"\n    group: "{{ item.group }}"\n    mode: "{{ item.mode }}"\n  with_items: "{{ rsyslog_additional_configs }}"\n\n- name: Start and enable rsyslog\n  service:\n    name: rsyslog\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-02T11:20:18.745363172Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 14415652557, 'load_duration': 92224869, 'promp