Task 2: Install fail2ban
Description Task 2: Install the fail2ban package using the list defined in the variable fail2ban_packages.

Task 3: Copy filters in filter.d
Description Task 3: Copy custom filter configuration files from the specified source path to the /etc/fail2ban/filter.d/ directory, setting appropriate permissions, and restart fail2ban service afterward.

Task 4: Configure fail2ban.local
Description Task 4: Update the fail2ban.local configuration file with the provided settings, ensuring proper permissions, and trigger a service restart after configuration changes.

Task 5: Configure jail.local
Description Task 5: Apply the specified jail configurations to the fail2ban jail.local file, setting correct permissions, and restart fail2ban after updating.

Task 6: Stat auth log file
Description Task 6: Check if the /var/log/auth.log file exists.

Task 7: Touch auth log file
Description Task 7: Create an empty /var/log/auth.log file if it does not exist and set appropriate permissions.

