el-next-release if needed.\n\nI also need to add a handler for updating the package cache. I'll define it at the end of the playbook with a meta module.\n\nNow, putting it all together, I'll structure each task with the appropriate module and parameters. I'll ensure that each task has the correct name and that the fourth task includes the condition and notify.\n\nI'll start the playbook with '---' followed by a list of tasks. Each task will have the correct module, name, state, and any other parameters. The handler will be defined at the end using the include_tasks or meta module to run the update.\n\nI should double-check the YAML syntax to avoid any errors. Also, ensure that the paths and URLs are correct, especially for the GPG key.\n\nFinally, I'll make sure there are no extra comments or explanations, just the valid YAML tasks as required.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Install epel\n  yum:\n    name: epel\n    state: present\n\n- name: Install epel gpg key\n  yum:\n    name: https://dl.fedoraproject.org/pub/epel/RPM-GPG-KEY-EPEL\n    state: gpgkey\n\n- name: Install epel-release\n  yum:\n    name: epel-release\n    state: present\n\n- name: Install epel-next-release\n  yum:\n    name: epel-next-release\n    state: present\n  when: epel_next\n  notify: update_package_cache\n\n- name: update_package_cache\n  meta: \n    main: false\n  handler: true\n  yum:\n    state: update_cache\n```" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-02T11:38:44.386961743Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 13292540584, 'load_duration': 78631302, 'prompt_eval_count': 375, 'prompt_eval_duration': 85233674, 'eval_count': 840, 'eval_duration': 13127104777, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--796a7b81-3ab7-432c-8c46-c540f34ecee9-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 375, 'output_tokens': 840, 'total_tokens': 1215}
